Two independent reproductions. Playwright page.route() intercepted the
POST http://localhost:8000/api/runs request and aborted it client-side
BEFORE it reached the backend (no real run was created), purely to inspect
the exact payload the browser had already assembled.

Repro 1 (brief text + valid.md + huge.txt attached):
  bodyLen: 450427
  containsTrunc (payload includes the word "truncat"): false
  huge.txt block present at offset 251, content is 'a' repeated with no
  truncation marker before "=== End: huge.txt ==="

Repro 2 (brief text + huge.txt only attached):
  bodyLen: 450236
  containsTrunc: false
  tail of body: "...aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
  \n=== End: huge.txt ===\",\"_display_title\":\"Summarize the attached notes into user stories.\"}"

Source: frontend/src/components/workflow/IdeaInputPage.tsx handleFiles():
  - isTextFile (.txt/.md/.json/.csv) path (line ~514-523): reads via
    FileReader, stores content.slice(0, ATTACH_MAX_CHARS) with NO
    truncation note appended.
  - isBinaryFile (.pdf/.docx/.pptx) path (line ~524-545): calls
    extractFileText(), and explicitly appends
    "\n[Content truncated to 450,000 chars]" when res.truncated is true.
  ATTACH_MAX_CHARS = 450000 (frontend/src/lib/constants.ts:7).

The attached-file chip UI (same file, ~line 629-639) renders only the
filename — no size, no truncation state — for both file-type paths, so
there is no UI signal at all that a text attachment's content was cut.
